@startuml
title F13 - Backup routing and delivery visibility
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
control "Hub routine deadline timer" as HubTimer
control "B04\nIncident workflow" as B04
control "B05\nNotification routing" as B05
participant "Web Push provider" as Push
actor "Primary caregiver" as Primary
actor "Backup caregiver" as Backup
boundary "A04\nApp incidents" as A04
boundary "A05\nApp platform" as A05
control "B08\nOperations/data" as B08
B04 -> B05: Create unique primary-now and backup-after-300s jobs
B05 -> Push: Submit primary route
Push --> B05: Return provider accepted/failed state
Push -> Primary: Attempt device delivery
B05 -> B08: Record provider result separately from human state
HubTimer -> B05: Backup delay expires while incident remains unacknowledged
B05 -> Push: Submit backup route once
Push -> Backup: Attempt backup delivery
Primary -> A04: Optional claim/acknowledge
A04 -> B04: Human acknowledgement closes pending route eligibility
A05 -> B08: Read provider, push capability and freshness diagnostics
note over Primary,Backup: The UI reports accepted, failed, pending and acknowledged states without assuming receipt.
note over HubTimer,B08: Outcome - Escalation is bounded and observable, with no duplicate route and no claim that a notification was seen.
@enduml
